Description: Reserve room for the whole padded string
 xo_format_string reserved room for the minimum width in bytes before it
 padded a string. A string can take more bytes than columns: multibyte
 characters, XML and HTML entities, and JSON and SD-PARAMS escapes. The
 padding then wrote past the end of the heap buffer. df pads each mount
 source to the byte length of the longest one, in text output and with
 --libxo.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-17

--- a/libxo/libxo.c
+++ b/libxo/libxo.c
@@ -10,6 +10,9 @@
  * Modified 2026-11-17: the XML, JSON and SD-PARAMS escapers reserve room
  * for the whole escaped string.
  *
+ * Modified 2026-11-17: padding a string to its minimum width reserves room
+ * for the whole padded string.
+ *
  * This is the implementation of libxo, the formatting library that
  * generates multiple styles of output from a single code path.
  * Command line utilities can have their normal text output while
@@ -3179,7 +3182,7 @@ xo_format_string (xo_handle_t *xop, xo_b
 	 * but if we did the work ourselves, then we need to do it.
 	 */
 	int delta = xfp->xf_width[XF_WIDTH_MIN] - cols;
-	if (!xo_buf_has_room(xbp, xfp->xf_width[XF_WIDTH_MIN]))
+	if (!xo_buf_has_room(xbp, rc + delta))
 	    goto bail;
 
